<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">3 </span>Experiments</h2>

<section id="S3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.1 </span>Tasks, Models, and Baselines</h3>

<section id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Tasks.</h4>

<div id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate OpenVLHarness across four task domains spanning 22 datasets, as summarized in Table <a href="#S3.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ Tasks. ‣ 3.1 Tasks, Models, and Baselines ‣ 3 Experiments ‣ OpenVLHarness: Real World Visual Agentic Tool-Use with Multimodal Memory" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> (splits, sizes, and scoring in Appendix <a href="#A4" title="Appendix D Benchmarks and Evaluation Protocol ‣ OpenVLHarness: Real World Visual Agentic Tool-Use with Multimodal Memory" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D</span></a>):</p>
<ul id="S3.I1" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:1.4em;">
<li id="S3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Grounded perception.</span> Five benchmarks targeting object counting and open-vocabulary visual grounding: CountQA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">Tamarapalli et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, FSC-147 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib66" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ranjan et al., 2021</a>)</cite>, OdinW-13-All <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al., 2022</a>)</cite>, FSCD-147 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">Nguyen et al., 2022</a>)</cite>, and FSCD-LVIS <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">Nguyen et al., 2022</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Visual search and deep research.</span> Six benchmarks drawn from a suite of 11 multimodal information-seeking tasks: FVQA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib53" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wu et al., 2025a</a>)</cite>, MMSearch <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">Jiang et al., 2024</a>)</cite>, MMSearch-Plus <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib45" title="" class="ltx_ref">Tao et al., 2026</a>)</cite>, HLE-VL <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib51" title="" class="ltx_ref">Phan et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, BrowseComp-VL <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib47" title="" class="ltx_ref">Geng et al., 2026</a>)</cite>, and RealX-Bench <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hong et al., 2026a</a>)</cite>; the remaining five are evaluated in Appendix <a href="#A2.SS5" title="B.5 Extended Visual Search and Deep Research Results ‣ Appendix B Additional Results and Analysis ‣ OpenVLHarness: Real World Visual Agentic Tool-Use with Multimodal Memory" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.5</span></a>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">General VQA and hallucination.</span> Six benchmarks covering general visual question answering and hallucination robustness: RealWorldQA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib65" title="" class="ltx_ref">xAI, 2024</a>)</cite>, SimpleVQA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib49" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cheng et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, HallusionBench <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib67" title="" class="ltx_ref">Guan et al., 2024</a>)</cite>, FREAK-VQA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib68" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yin et al., 2026</a>)</cite>, FREAK-MCQ <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib68" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yin et al., 2026</a>)</cite>, and V* <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib74" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wu and Xie, 2024</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Spatial reasoning.</span> Five benchmarks targeting spatial and embodied reasoning: MMSI-Bench <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib69" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yang et al., 2025b</a>)</cite>, ERQA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib70" title="" class="ltx_ref">Team et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, EmbSpatial-Bench <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib71" title="" class="ltx_ref">Du et al., 2024</a>)</cite>, SparBench <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib72" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al., 2026a</a>)</cite>, and MindCube <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib73" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al., 2025c</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
