<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Models and baselines.</h4>

<div id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We instantiate OpenVLHarness on four open-source models across different sizes—Qwen2.5-VL-7B-Instruct <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib58" title="" class="ltx_ref">Qwen Team, 2025a</a>)</cite>, Qwen3-VL-8B-Instruct <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib57" title="" class="ltx_ref">Qwen Team, 2025b</a>)</cite>, Qwen3-VL-32B-Instruct, and Kimi K3 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib111" title="" class="ltx_ref">Team et al., 2026</a>)</cite>—and four proprietary models: GPT-5 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib91" title="" class="ltx_ref">OpenAI, 2025b</a>)</cite>, GPT-6 Luna, GPT-6 Sol, and GPT-6 Astra <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib92" title="" class="ltx_ref">OpenAI, 2026</a>)</cite>. Per-model sampling parameters can be found in Appendix <a href="#A3.SS6" title="C.6 Models and Serving ‣ Appendix C Harness Implementation Details ‣ OpenVLHarness: Real World Visual Agentic Tool-Use with Multimodal Memory" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.6</span></a>. Because the search APIs, the agent’s tool-routing decisions, and the LLM judge are all stochastic, every Qwen3-VL result, for OpenVLHarness and for all baselines, is the mean of <em id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">three</em> independent runs with different random seeds, while results with proprietary backbones are single runs because of API cost (standard deviations in Appendix <a href="#A8" title="Appendix H Run-to-Run Variability ‣ OpenVLHarness: Real World Visual Agentic Tool-Use with Multimodal Memory" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H</span></a>). In addition to the no-tool baseline (denoted <span id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Base</span>), we compare OpenVLHarness against two groups of baselines: <span id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Training-based baselines</span>: AdaReasoner <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Song et al., 2026</a>)</cite>, PixelReasoner <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al., 2025a</a>)</cite>, and DeepEyesV2 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hong et al., 2026a</a>)</cite>—harnesses that require fine-tuning the backbone to adapt it to the tool-use framework—evaluated with their released Qwen2.5-VL-7B checkpoints (Appendix Table <a href="#A2.T9" title="Table 9 ‣ B.3 Training-Based Baselines ‣ Appendix B Additional Results and Analysis ‣ OpenVLHarness: Real World Visual Agentic Tool-Use with Multimodal Memory" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>; setup in Appendix <a href="#A7.SS2" title="G.2 Training-Based Harnesses ‣ Appendix G Baseline Reproduction ‣ OpenVLHarness: Real World Visual Agentic Tool-Use with Multimodal Memory" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G.2</span></a>). <span id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Training-free baselines</span>: Visual Sketchpad <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hu et al., 2024</a>)</cite> and OctoTools <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lu et al., 2025</a>)</cite> are visual tool-use harnesses evaluated on the same Qwen3-VL backbones as OpenVLHarness (detailed setup in Appendix <a href="#A7.SS1" title="G.1 Training-Free Harnesses ‣ Appendix G Baseline Reproduction ‣ OpenVLHarness: Real World Visual Agentic Tool-Use with Multimodal Memory" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G.1</span></a>). We additionally evaluate Visual Sketchpad and Codex on GPT-6 Luna.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.2 </span>Main Results</h3>

<div id="S3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Across the evaluated backbones, OpenVLHarness improves average performance over the underlying base model and outperforms all existing training-free harnesses (Table <a href="#S3.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ Tasks. ‣ 3.1 Tasks, Models, and Baselines ‣ 3 Experiments ‣ OpenVLHarness: Real World Visual Agentic Tool-Use with Multimodal Memory" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>). On Qwen3-VL-8B, it raises the 22-dataset average from <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="34.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>34.2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">34.2</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="45.4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>45.4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">45.4</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="S3.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+11.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>11.2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+11.2</annotation></semantics></math>), exceeding the strongest training-free baseline, OctoTools (<math id="S3.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="31.8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>31.8</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">31.8</annotation></semantics></math>), by <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="13.6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>13.6</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">13.6</annotation></semantics></math> points; on Qwen3-VL-32B, the average rises from <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="38.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>38.3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">38.3</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="50.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>50.9</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">50.9</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="S3.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+12.6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>12.6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+12.6</annotation></semantics></math>). The gains extend to GPT-5 (<math id="S3.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="44.4\!\to\!55.7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>55.7</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">44.4\!\to\!55.7</annotation></semantics></math>), GPT-6 Sol (<math id="S3.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="52.7\!\to\!64.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>64.3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">52.7\!\to\!64.3</annotation></semantics></math>), and Kimi K3 (<math id="S3.SS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="56.4\!\to\!66.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>66.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">56.4\!\to\!66.1</annotation></semantics></math>) (Appendix Table <a href="#A2.T7" title="Table 7 ‣ B.1 Additional Backbones ‣ Appendix B Additional Results and Analysis ‣ OpenVLHarness: Real World Visual Agentic Tool-Use with Multimodal Memory" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>). On the Qwen2.5-VL-7B backbone, OpenVLHarness averages <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="33.45" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>33.45</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">33.45</annotation></semantics></math> across the 22 datasets, surpassing the training-based baselines AdaReasoner (<math id="S3.SS2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="25.29" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>25.29</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">25.29</annotation></semantics></math>), PixelReasoner (<math id="S3.SS2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="28.02" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>28.02</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">28.02</annotation></semantics></math>), and DeepEyesV2 (<math id="S3.SS2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="25.02" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>25.02</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">25.02</annotation></semantics></math>), without updating model weights (Appendix Table <a href="#A2.T9" title="Table 9 ‣ B.3 Training-Based Baselines ‣ Appendix B Additional Results and Analysis ‣ OpenVLHarness: Real World Visual Agentic Tool-Use with Multimodal Memory" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The GPT-6 results highlight that effective multimodal tool use depends on the harness. With GPT-6 Luna, Codex averages <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="43.8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>43.8</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">43.8</annotation></semantics></math>, below the no-tool baseline (<math id="S3.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="45.8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>45.8</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">45.8</annotation></semantics></math>), while OpenVLHarness reaches <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="56.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>56.5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">56.5</annotation></semantics></math>. This comparison shows that a coding-agent harness does not automatically improve multimodal reasoning. With GPT-6 Astra, OpenVLHarness improves all 22 benchmarks and raises the average from <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="60.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>60.3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">60.3</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="70.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>70.2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">70.2</annotation></semantics></math>, the highest of any backbone.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Grounded perception and visual search and deep research benefit substantially from dedicated vision experts and external retrieval, respectively. Gains on general VQA and hallucination and on spatial reasoning depend more on the backbone: Luna and Astra improve on every benchmark in these domains (Luna by less than one point on RealWorldQA, HallusionBench, and EmbSpatial), with average gains of <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+6.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>6.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+6.5</annotation></semantics></math>/<math id="S3.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+7.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>7.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+7.5</annotation></semantics></math> on general VQA and hallucination and <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+6.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>6.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+6.5</annotation></semantics></math>/<math id="S3.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+5.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>5.2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+5.2</annotation></semantics></math> on spatial reasoning, respectively. This pattern is consistent with greater proficiency in using tools and reasoning over their visual evidence. The less consistent gains on Qwen3-VL-8B motivate the failure analysis and domain specialization in Secs. <a href="#S3.SS5" title="3.5 Failure Analysis ‣ 3 Experiments ‣ OpenVLHarness: Real World Visual Agentic Tool-Use with Multimodal Memory" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.5</span></a> and <a href="#S3.SS6" title="3.6 Harness Optimization ‣ 3 Experiments ‣ OpenVLHarness: Real World Visual Agentic Tool-Use with Multimodal Memory" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.6</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
