</section>
<section id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Per-capability effects.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#A1.F8" title="Figure 8 ‣ Null control. ‣ A.3 Effect of Tool Use on Accuracy ‣ Appendix A Tool-Use Behavior ‣ OpenVLHarness: Real World Visual Agentic Tool-Use with Multimodal Memory" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> reports, for each capability
and model, the paired difference on the questions that invoked it.
Table <a href="#A1.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ Per-capability effects. ‣ A.3 Effect of Tool Use on Accuracy ‣ Appendix A Tool-Use Behavior ‣ OpenVLHarness: Real World Visual Agentic Tool-Use with Multimodal Memory" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> gives the underlying counts, the share of questions each capability
was invoked on, the accuracies of both arms, and the control, that is the same difference on the
questions that did not invoke the capability. The two retrieval
capabilities exhibit the largest separation from their controls in every model: rows invoking Image
Search improve by <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="18.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>18.9</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">18.9</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="27.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>27.1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">27.1</annotation></semantics></math> points, while the corresponding control values lie between <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-0.6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-0.6</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+6.6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>6.6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+6.6</annotation></semantics></math>. Visual Grounding is the dominant factor for the smaller models — Qwen3-VL-8B improves by <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="14.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>14.3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">14.3</annotation></semantics></math>
points on rows that ground and declines by <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="20.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>20.1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">20.1</annotation></semantics></math> points on rows that do not — and flattens for the
larger models, which invoke it on nearly all questions. Camera Trajectory is positive for all five
models. Depth Estimation, OCR, Zoom-in and the Python Coding Agent are at or below their controls, apart
from Zoom-in for GPT-6 Luna (<math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+11.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>11.9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+11.9</annotation></semantics></math> against <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+8.6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>8.6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+8.6</annotation></semantics></math>) and GPT-6 Astra (<math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+9.4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>9.4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+9.4</annotation></semantics></math> against <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+5.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>5.2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+5.2</annotation></semantics></math>), which
is consistent with their being invoked on the questions a model cannot resolve from the image alone
rather than with their being ineffective in isolation.</p>
</div>
