<section id="A1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.4 </span>Capability Composition</h3>

<section id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Composition across capabilities.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Rollouts frequently combine several capabilities rather
than invoking one in isolation. Counting the number of <em id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">distinct</em> capabilities per rollout, among
engaged rollouts <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="31.9\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>31.9</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">31.9\%</annotation></semantics></math> (Qwen3-VL-32B), <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="26.8\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>26.8</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">26.8\%</annotation></semantics></math> (GPT-6 Sol) and <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="26.0\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>26.0</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">26.0\%</annotation></semantics></math> (GPT-6 Astra) invoke two or more, against <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="20.7\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>20.7</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">20.7\%</annotation></semantics></math>
and <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="11.6\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>11.6</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">11.6\%</annotation></semantics></math> for the smaller models, and the longest rollouts combine four or five. Combinations that
cross capability families are rarer, <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="16\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">16\%</annotation></semantics></math> of engaged rollouts, and consist almost entirely of a
perception capability followed by the Python Coding Agent: ground or measure first, then compute over the
resulting quantities. This is the pattern rewarded by the counting, grounding and spatial datasets, and
it is not expressible in a harness that exposes a single capability.</p>
</div>
