<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Additional Results and Analysis</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section reports results with additional backbones (GPT-5, GPT-6 Sol, and Kimi K3), gives details of the ablation in Table <a href="#S3.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ 3.4 Ablation Study ‣ 3 Experiments ‣ OpenVLHarness: Real World Visual Agentic Tool-Use with Multimodal Memory" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, compares OpenVLHarness with training-based harnesses, analyzes grounded perception across object counts, extends the visual search and deep research results to <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="11" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>11</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">11</annotation></semantics></math> information-seeking benchmarks, and tests whether additional reasoning can replace the harness.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Additional Backbones</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A2.T7" title="Table 7 ‣ B.1 Additional Backbones ‣ Appendix B Additional Results and Analysis ‣ OpenVLHarness: Real World Visual Agentic Tool-Use with Multimodal Memory" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> evaluates OpenVLHarness with GPT-5 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib91" title="" class="ltx_ref">OpenAI, 2025b</a>)</cite>, with GPT-6 Sol <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib92" title="" class="ltx_ref">OpenAI, 2026</a>)</cite>, and with Kimi K3 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib111" title="" class="ltx_ref">Team et al., 2026</a>)</cite>, an open-weight mixture-of-experts model with native visual understanding, on the same <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="22" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>22</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">22</annotation></semantics></math> datasets as Table <a href="#S3.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ Tasks. ‣ 3.1 Tasks, Models, and Baselines ‣ 3 Experiments ‣ OpenVLHarness: Real World Visual Agentic Tool-Use with Multimodal Memory" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, using the same tools, memory, prompts, and scoring. With GPT-6 Sol, OpenVLHarness improves every one of the <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="22" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>22</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">22</annotation></semantics></math> benchmarks, raising the average from <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="52.7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>52.7</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">52.7</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="64.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>64.3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">64.3</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
