</figure>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Ablation Study Details</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The ablation in Table <a href="#S3.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ 3.4 Ablation Study ‣ 3 Experiments ‣ OpenVLHarness: Real World Visual Agentic Tool-Use with Multimodal Memory" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> isolates the contribution of each harness component by building a strict superset ladder: every rung adds exactly one mechanism to the one below it, so the gap between adjacent rungs measures that mechanism’s marginal value.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Variants.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The five rungs are:</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ol id="A2.I1" class="ltx_enumerate" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:1.4em;">
<li id="A2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Baseline (no tool).</span> The backbone model prompted directly with the question image and no tool access, establishing the no-harness floor.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">+ Tool.</span> The nine tools are available, but their payloads arrive as raw dumps, their schema is cut to a minimal signature (name, argument names and types, one clause each), and nothing persists between turns: no environment updates, no image labels, no data bindings, no URL references. Tool-generated images are replaced by a short stub.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">+ Capability layer.</span> Adds the capability layer of Sec. <a href="#S2.SS1" title="2.1 Capability Layer ‣ 2 Harness Design ‣ OpenVLHarness: Real World Visual Agentic Tool-Use with Multimodal Memory" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a>: each tool’s raw payload is replaced by a per-tool post-processor that condenses it into a concise, model-readable summary (e.g. grounding boxes on a 0–1000 grid, reranked search results with inline citations, depth/zoom captions), and the full tool schema is restored so the model is told when to reach for each tool and how to phrase its arguments. No memory is present—nothing is carried across turns.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">+ Textual memory.</span> Adds every memory mechanism that is addressed by a <em id="A2.I1.i4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">text</em> handle: per-turn Environment Updates that re-advertise all live state, <span id="A2.I1.i4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">webpage_url_N</span> references that let the agent revisit a URL, and out-of-context data bindings that the Python Coding Agent can read as typed variables. Tool-generated images are replaced by a VLM-written text description (up to 160 tokens) conditioned on the original question. Image references remain absent: tool-produced images cannot be named, stored, or passed to a later tool call.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">5.</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">OpenVLHarness (full).</span> Adds multimodal image memory: every tool-produced image is labeled (<span id="A2.I1.i5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">tool_generated_image_N</span>), deduplicated by content, and kept addressable. The model selects which image to pass to each tool call by its identifier, enabling compositions such as grounding <math id="A2.I1.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\to" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\to</annotation></semantics></math> zoom <math id="A2.I1.i5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\to" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\to</annotation></semantics></math> OCR <math id="A2.I1.i5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\to" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\to</annotation></semantics></math> search.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Implementation.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">All five variants share the same nine-tool toolset, backbone weights, and decoding configuration (temperature <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.7</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.7</annotation></semantics></math>, top-<math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.8</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.8</annotation></semantics></math>, top-<math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>20</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">20</annotation></semantics></math>, repetition penalty <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.0</annotation></semantics></math>, presence penalty <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.5</annotation></semantics></math>, up to <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="12{,}800" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>12,800</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">12{,}800</annotation></semantics></math> generated tokens per turn, <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="15" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>15</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">15</annotation></semantics></math> tool-calling iterations, <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="168" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>168</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">168</annotation></semantics></math>K-token context cap). They differ only in the <em id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">ablation preset</em> applied to the memory stack: a configuration block that switches individual mechanisms (environment updates, image identifiers, per-tool post-processors, data bindings, URL references) on or off. Each preset is a strict superset of the one below it, validated at initialization so a typo fails the run rather than silently selecting the wrong baseline. Table <a href="#A2.T8" title="Table 8 ‣ Implementation. ‣ B.2 Ablation Study Details ‣ Appendix B Additional Results and Analysis ‣ OpenVLHarness: Real World Visual Agentic Tool-Use with Multimodal Memory" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> summarizes the knob settings for each variant.</p>
</div>
