<section id="A2.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.5 </span>Extended Visual Search and Deep Research Results</h3>

<div id="A2.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A2.T12" title="Table 12 ‣ B.5 Extended Visual Search and Deep Research Results ‣ Appendix B Additional Results and Analysis ‣ OpenVLHarness: Real World Visual Agentic Tool-Use with Multimodal Memory" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a> extends the search results to <math id="A2.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="11" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>11</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">11</annotation></semantics></math> information-seeking benchmarks, including five that are not in Table <a href="#S3.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ Tasks. ‣ 3.1 Tasks, Models, and Baselines ‣ 3 Experiments ‣ OpenVLHarness: Real World Visual Agentic Tool-Use with Multimodal Memory" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. The agent workflow improves every backbone: the average across the <math id="A2.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="11" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>11</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">11</annotation></semantics></math> benchmarks rises from <math id="A2.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="13.74" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>13.74</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">13.74</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A2.SS5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="29.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>29.05</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">29.05</annotation></semantics></math> for Qwen3-VL-8B, from <math id="A2.SS5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="19.21" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>19.21</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">19.21</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A2.SS5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="34.61" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>34.61</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">34.61</annotation></semantics></math> for Qwen3-VL-32B, and from <math id="A2.SS5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="31.58" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>31.58</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">31.58</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A2.SS5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="41.80" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>41.80</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">41.80</annotation></semantics></math> for GPT-5. Gains are largest for the open models, whose parametric knowledge is most limited; GPT-5’s direct-inference accuracy is additionally depressed by refusals on identity queries (Appendix <a href="#A4.SS2.SSS0.Px15" title="Refusals on identity queries. ‣ D.2 Visual Search and Deep Research ‣ Appendix D Benchmarks and Evaluation Protocol ‣ OpenVLHarness: Real World Visual Agentic Tool-Use with Multimodal Memory" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a>). With the harness, Qwen3-VL-32B surpasses direct GPT-5 on average (<math id="A2.SS5.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="34.61" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>34.61</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">34.61</annotation></semantics></math> vs. <math id="A2.SS5.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="31.58" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>31.58</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">31.58</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div>
