<section id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Results.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Raising the effort increases the 22-benchmark average of every method. OpenVLHarness at medium effort (<math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="56.52" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>56.52</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">56.52</annotation></semantics></math> at $0.92 per <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1{,}000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1,000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1{,}000</annotation></semantics></math> questions) exceeds every setting of every other method by at least <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="7.68" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>7.68</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">7.68</annotation></semantics></math> points; the strongest of those settings is Visual Sketchpad at max effort (<math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="48.84" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>48.84</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">48.84</annotation></semantics></math> at $5.15). OpenVLHarness at low effort (<math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="49.92" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>49.92</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">49.92</annotation></semantics></math> at $0.64) already exceeds the average of every other setting. At low effort, OpenVLHarness leads Base on grounded perception and on visual search and deep research but trails it on general VQA and hallucination and on spatial reasoning (<math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="61.51" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>61.51</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">61.51</annotation></semantics></math> vs. <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="61.63" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>61.63</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">61.63</annotation></semantics></math>; <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="54.45" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>54.45</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">54.45</annotation></semantics></math> vs. <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="56.54" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>56.54</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">56.54</annotation></semantics></math>); from medium effort onward, it leads Base in every domain. At max effort, the gap between OpenVLHarness (<math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="60.12" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>60.12</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">60.12</annotation></semantics></math> at $2.99) and the best other method is largest on grounded perception (<math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="15.6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>15.6</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">15.6</annotation></semantics></math> points) and on visual search and deep research (<math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="12.4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>12.4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">12.4</annotation></semantics></math>), consistent with the harness supplying evidence that the model cannot infer from the image, and smaller on general VQA and hallucination (<math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="6.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>6.1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6.1</annotation></semantics></math>) and on spatial reasoning (<math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="7.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>7.1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">7.1</annotation></semantics></math>). Returns per unit of cost diminish for Base: moving from xhigh to max effort multiplies its cost by <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2.7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2.7</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2.7</annotation></semantics></math> and raises its average by <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.72" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.72</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.72</annotation></semantics></math> points. On FSC-147, no other setting exceeds <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="38.34" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>38.34</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">38.34</annotation></semantics></math>, against <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="40.59" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>40.59</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">40.59</annotation></semantics></math> for OpenVLHarness at low effort; on the six search benchmarks, OpenVLHarness at max effort exceeds the best other setting by <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3.0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3.0</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="19.6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>19.6</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">19.6</annotation></semantics></math> points, and OpenVLHarness at low effort already exceeds it on <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math> of them. OpenVLHarness attains the best score of all settings on <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>20</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">20</annotation></semantics></math> of the <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="22" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>22</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">22</annotation></semantics></math> benchmarks; the exceptions are HallusionBench (Codex at xhigh effort, <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="69.89" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>69.89</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">69.89</annotation></semantics></math>, against <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="69.66" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>69.66</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">69.66</annotation></semantics></math> for OpenVLHarness at max effort) and ERQA (Visual Sketchpad at max effort, <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="64.75" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>64.75</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">64.75</annotation></semantics></math>, against <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p1.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="63.50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>63.50</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">63.50</annotation></semantics></math> for OpenVLHarness at max effort).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Token usage.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Most input tokens of OpenVLHarness, Codex, and Visual Sketchpad are cache reads and writes of the context carried across their model calls, whereas Base sends a single prompt. For Base, raising the effort leaves the input unchanged at about <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1{,}800" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1,800</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1{,}800</annotation></semantics></math> tokens per question and mainly increases reasoning tokens, from <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="301" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>301</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">301</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5{,}852" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5,852</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5{,}852</annotation></semantics></math> per question between low and max effort. For the three harnesses, the input also grows between low and max effort: from about <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8{,}000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>8,000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8{,}000</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="11{,}800" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>11,800</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">11{,}800</annotation></semantics></math> tokens per question for Codex, from <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="20{,}800" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>20,800</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">20{,}800</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="24{,}100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>24,100</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">24{,}100</annotation></semantics></math> for Visual Sketchpad, and from <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="14{,}500" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>14,500</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">14{,}500</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="24{,}600" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>24,600</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">24{,}600</annotation></semantics></math> for OpenVLHarness.</p>
</div>
