<section id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Code execution in Codex.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The sandbox permits code execution at every setting, yet GPT-6 Luna rarely uses it: Codex executes at least one command on <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.16\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.16</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.16\%</annotation></semantics></math> of questions at low effort and <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="6.17\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>6.17</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6.17\%</annotation></semantics></math> at max effort (Table <a href="#A2.T15" title="Table 15 ‣ Code execution in Codex. ‣ B.6 Reasoning-Effort Study: Setup and Full Results ‣ Appendix B Additional Results and Analysis ‣ OpenVLHarness: Real World Visual Agentic Tool-Use with Multimodal Memory" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>). Execution concentrates on grounded perception and on visual search and deep research (<math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="12.3\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>12.3</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">12.3\%</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="9.6\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>9.6</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">9.6\%</annotation></semantics></math> of their questions at max effort) and is almost absent on general VQA and hallucination and on spatial reasoning. On most questions, Codex therefore reduces to the model answering directly within the Codex agent loop and prompt. Its average is at most <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2.0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2.0</annotation></semantics></math> points below that of Base from medium to xhigh effort and <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.5</annotation></semantics></math> points above it at max effort, but <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="7.4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>7.4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">7.4</annotation></semantics></math> points below it at low effort; this drop is not caused by failed requests, since every question receives a non-empty answer.</p>
</div>
