<div id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A2.T17" title="Table 17 ‣ Setup. ‣ B.7 Codex with Open-Source Backbones ‣ Appendix B Additional Results and Analysis ‣ OpenVLHarness: Real World Visual Agentic Tool-Use with Multimodal Memory" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a> reports the results. Averaged over the <math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="22" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>22</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">22</annotation></semantics></math> benchmarks, Codex scores below Base with both backbones: <math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="31.42" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>31.42</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">31.42</annotation></semantics></math> vs. <math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="34.24" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>34.24</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">34.24</annotation></semantics></math> with Qwen3-VL-8B and <math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="36.46" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>36.46</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">36.46</annotation></semantics></math> vs. <math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="38.30" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>38.30</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">38.30</annotation></semantics></math> with Qwen3-VL-32B, while OpenVLHarness reaches <math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="45.41" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>45.41</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">45.41</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="50.92" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>50.92</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">50.92</annotation></semantics></math>. Codex beats Base on <math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math> benchmarks with the 8B model and <math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>7</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">7</annotation></semantics></math> with the 32B model. The larger gains are on RealX-Bench, FVQA, and MMSearch-Plus, on MindCube (<math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+1.35" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1.35</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+1.35</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+3.47" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>3.47</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+3.47</annotation></semantics></math> points), and on FREAK-MCQ with the 32B model (<math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+6.04" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>6.04</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+6.04</annotation></semantics></math>); the other gains are below <math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.5</annotation></semantics></math> points. The largest losses are on V* (<math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-14.13" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>14.13</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-14.13</annotation></semantics></math> points with the 8B model), BC-VL (<math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-7.52" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>7.52</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-7.52</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-11.53" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>11.53</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-11.53</annotation></semantics></math>), SimpleVQA (<math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-8.06" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>8.06</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-8.06</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-8.88" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>8.88</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-8.88</annotation></semantics></math>), and OdinW-13-All (<math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-6.10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6.10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-6.10</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-7.73" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>7.73</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-7.73</annotation></semantics></math>). OpenVLHarness scores above Codex on every benchmark with the 8B model and on <math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>20</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">20</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="22" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>22</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">22</annotation></semantics></math> with the 32B model. The two exceptions are FREAK-MCQ (<math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="50.10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>50.10</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">50.10</annotation></semantics></math> vs. <math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="45.77" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>45.77</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">45.77</annotation></semantics></math>) and SparBench (<math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="46.99" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>46.99</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">46.99</annotation></semantics></math> vs. <math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="46.76" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>46.76</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">46.76</annotation></semantics></math>). As with GPT-6 Luna, placing a model in a general-purpose coding-agent loop does not by itself reproduce the gains of OpenVLHarness.</p>
</div>
