<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Harness Implementation Details</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section documents the harness of Section <a href="#S2" title="2 Harness Design ‣ OpenVLHarness: Real World Visual Agentic Tool-Use with Multimodal Memory" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>: the nine capabilities of Section <a href="#S2.SS1" title="2.1 Capability Layer ‣ 2 Harness Design ‣ OpenVLHarness: Real World Visual Agentic Tool-Use with Multimodal Memory" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a>, how their outputs are kept in multimodal memory, and the agent’s system prompt.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Capabilities and backends.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Following the generalized capability abstraction of Section <a href="#S2.SS1" title="2.1 Capability Layer ‣ 2 Harness Design ‣ OpenVLHarness: Real World Visual Agentic Tool-Use with Multimodal Memory" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a>, each capability exposes a fixed interface to the agent: typed arguments in, and a natural-language message plus memory artifacts out. The expert model or service behind the interface is a configurable backend, and switching it changes neither the agent’s prompt, the tool schema, nor the memory interface. Table <a href="#A3.T18" title="Table 18 ‣ Capabilities and backends. ‣ Appendix C Harness Implementation Details ‣ OpenVLHarness: Real World Visual Agentic Tool-Use with Multimodal Memory" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a> lists the capabilities and their backends; all experiments in this paper use the default backend of each capability, shown in bold.</p>
</div>
