<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Search Tools</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">By default, all three search tools route queries through the Serper API<span id="footnote1" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">1</span>
              
              
              
            <a href="https://serper.dev/" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://serper.dev/</a></span></span></span>; Text Search and Image Search can instead be served by Gemini <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib107" title="" class="ltx_ref">Comanici and others, 2025</a>)</cite> with Google Search grounding, a costlier but stronger route. The search tools post-process the raw payload with a Qwen3-VL-8B-Instruct model as the VLM summarizer. The summarizer runs at decoding temperature <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> with a <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4096" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4096</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4096</annotation></semantics></math>-token output cap, and each call retrieves the top <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>10</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10</annotation></semantics></math> raw results before reranking and summarization.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Text Search.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Search the web with intelligent query routing and VLM summarization. Given a text query, the tool automatically classifies the query intent and routes it to the most appropriate Serper endpoint, which has general web, news, academic papers, images, maps, local places, shopping, or patents types, and returns a coherent summary of the top-<math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>10</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10</annotation></semantics></math> raw results with inline citations <span id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">[1], [2], …</span> followed by a citations block of source titles and URLs. This format supports multi-round search: the agent can read the summary for quick understanding and then visit specific cited URLs through Webpage Visit. The summarizer prompt is shown below.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="412.69" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 412.69" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,412.69) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#404040;" fill="#404040" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 406.79 C 0 410.05 2.64 412.69 5.91 412.69 L 544.09 412.69 C 547.36 412.69 550 410.05 550 406.79 L 550 5.91 C 550 2.64 547.36 0 544.09 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F2F2F2;" fill="#F2F2F2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 387.04 L 548.03 387.04 L 548.03 5.91 C 548.03 3.73 546.27 1.97 544.09 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 396.41)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.62em;">
<span id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Text Search summarizer prompt (abridged)</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 13.78)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:26.12em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="361.46" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 361.46)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.62em;">
<span id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">You are a research summarizer. Given raw web search results and a user query, do exactly three things:</span></span>
<span id="A3.I1" class="ltx_enumerate ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<span id="A3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<span id="A3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">RERANK the numbered organic results by how directly each helps answer the query.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<span id="A3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">KEEP at most </span><math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> most useful results; emit their original 1-based ranks as </span><span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">kept_indices</span><span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. If none help, emit </span><span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">kept_indices: []</span><span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A3.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<span id="A3.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A3.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">SUMMARIZE the query-relevant facts from the FULL set of raw results into a concise 3–5 sentence prose paragraph; include named entities, numbers, and dates verbatim.</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Knowledge-graph, answer-box, and top-stories blocks are ineligible for <span id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.pic1.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">kept_indices</span> but their facts should still surface in <span id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.pic1.2.2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">summary</span>. Output STRICT JSON with the schema <span id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.pic1.2.2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">{kept_indices, summary, no_results_justification, suggested_queries, suggested_next_actions}</span>; when no result is useful, populate the justification and propose alternative queries or downstream tool calls.</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Image Search.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Identify the objects, landmarks, artwork, text, products, plants, animals, and other entities depicted in an image, using Serper’s reverse-image-search (Google Lens) endpoint. Returns a list of visual matches with titles, source URLs, links, and thumbnails. The agent invokes the tool by passing the runtime identifier of the target image. The tool performs reverse search (image <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> information) on a single image per call; finding images from a text description is instead handled by Text Search with an image-search intent. A separate multimodal summarizer prompt (below) reranks the candidates against the query image and produces the same JSON envelope as Text Search.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="335.82" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 335.82" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,335.82) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#404040;" fill="#404040" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 329.91 C 0 333.18 2.64 335.82 5.91 335.82 L 544.09 335.82 C 547.36 335.82 550 333.18 550 329.91 L 550 5.91 C 550 2.64 547.36 0 544.09 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F2F2F2;" fill="#F2F2F2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 310.17 L 548.03 310.17 L 548.03 5.91 C 548.03 3.73 546.27 1.97 544.09 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 319.54)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.62em;">
<span id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Image Search summarizer prompt (abridged)</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 16.47)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:20.37em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="284.58" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 281.89)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.62em;">
<span id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">You are a visual-match summarizer. Given raw reverse-image-search results (and, in the multimodal variant, the query image plus each candidate’s thumbnail), do exactly three things:</span></span>
<span id="A3.I2" class="ltx_enumerate ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<span id="A3.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<span id="A3.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A3.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">RERANK the numbered matches by how likely each identifies the same subject as the query image.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A3.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<span id="A3.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A3.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">KEEP at most </span><math id="A3.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I2.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> most useful matches as </span><span id="A3.I2.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">kept_indices</span><span id="A3.I2.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A3.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<span id="A3.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A3.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">SUMMARIZE what the FULL set of raw matches indicates about the query image’s likely subject in a concise 3–5 sentence prose paragraph; capture entity names, dates, attributes verbatim.</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Output STRICT JSON with <span id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.pic1.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">{kept_indices, summary, no_results_justification, suggested_next_actions}</span>; when no match is useful, justify per-match and propose follow-up actions such as cropping with Visual Grounding before re-searching, or switching to Text Search.</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Webpage Visit.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Visit one or more webpages, convert them to plain text via Serper APIs, and extract goal-relevant content using a local Qwen3-VL-8B-Instruct model. This tool returns per-URL evidence and a summary. The extraction prompt is shown below.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="449.21" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 449.21" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,449.21) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#404040;" fill="#404040" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 443.3 C 0 446.56 2.64 449.21 5.91 449.21 L 544.09 449.21 C 547.36 449.21 550 446.56 550 443.3 L 550 5.91 C 550 2.64 547.36 0 544.09 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F2F2F2;" fill="#F2F2F2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 425.1 L 548.03 425.1 L 548.03 5.91 C 548.03 3.73 546.27 1.97 544.09 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 433.69)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.62em;">
<span id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Webpage Visit extraction prompt</span></span>
