<section id="A5.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.4 </span>Optimized Harnesses and Generated Tools</h3>

<section id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Harness text edits.</h4>

<div id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The RealWorldQA example below combines edits from three search rounds: five system-prompt additions and one addition to the Visual Grounding output template. They guide the orchestrator to inspect small road-scene details, verify counts, and match its visual conclusion to the answer options. The output-template edit illustrates how evidence rendering supports adaptation: it prompts verification of grounded candidates before they are used as counts or relation evidence.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="592.19" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 592.19" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,592.19) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#404040;" fill="#404040" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 586.28 C 0 589.54 2.64 592.19 5.91 592.19 L 544.09 592.19 C 547.36 592.19 550 589.54 550 586.28 L 550 5.91 C 550 2.64 547.36 0 544.09 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F2F2F2;" fill="#F2F2F2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 566.54 L 548.03 566.54 L 548.03 5.91 C 548.03 3.73 546.27 1.97 544.09 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 575.9)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.62em;">
<span id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Edits in a top-scoring RealWorldQA harness (additions only)</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 13.78)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:39.09em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="540.96" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 540.96)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.62em;">
<span id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">System prompt, when to use visual tools.<span id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.pic1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> For road-scene details such as traffic lights, traffic signs, arrows, lane markings, and whether a driver must stop, use visual tools before answering unless the relevant mark or signal is unmistakably large and clear. Before answering that such a detail is absent, not visible, or has a particular color/direction, ground the likely object or region and inspect the original pixels with zoom if the region is small or distant.</span></span></span>
<span id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">System prompt, using tool results.<span id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.pic1.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> For count questions with numeric options, compare the filtered candidate count with the option values. If the count is outside the listed values or directly adjacent to a listed value, do one missed-object check using a broader/simple phrase or one targeted zoom of the most uncertain region, then choose the listed option best supported by all evidence.</span></span></span>
<span id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">For counts of printed letters, digits, or symbols, use OCR or a text-focused zoom when available before deciding the count. Unless the question explicitly says “standalone”, count occurrences inside longer strings as well as isolated characters.</span></span>
<span id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">System prompt, final answer.<span id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.pic1.2.4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> For multiple-choice questions, before writing <span id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.pic1.2.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;answer&gt;</span>, explicitly bind your visual conclusion to the option table. The option letter and option text you output must match each other and match the conclusion in your thinking; if your conclusion is not one of the options, re-check the evidence instead of choosing a nearby option.</span></span></span>
<span id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.pic1.2.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">If the listed options do not include a none/unknown/cannot-determine choice, never use an unlisted absence answer such as “none of the above”, “not visible”, or “cannot tell”. If your draft conclusion is that the needed cue is absent, do one targeted visual check when a tool can resolve it, then answer with the listed option best supported by the evidence.</span></span>
<span id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.pic1.2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.pic1.2.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Visual Grounding output template<span id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.pic1.2.6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> (appended after the list of boxes). Treat these as candidate regions, not a verified final count. Before answering count, presence, or relation questions, compare each candidate with the original image and remove duplicates, mirror/reflection copies, partial regions, off-target detections, and objects that fail the question’s location or context constraint.</span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Task-specific tools.</h4>

<div id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A5.T24" title="Table 24 ‣ Task-specific tools. ‣ E.4 Optimized Harnesses and Generated Tools ‣ Appendix E Failure Analysis and Harness Optimization Details ‣ OpenVLHarness: Real World Visual Agentic Tool-Use with Multimodal Memory" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a> lists the five accepted tools: two from SparBench failures and three from FREAK-MCQ failures. A fourth FREAK direction, localized text and symbol reading, encountered an execution error before completing the gate. The SparBench tools package depth, camera intrinsics, and cross-view geometry into metric 3D operations, addressing the composition needs of channel C. In the diagnosed SparBench failures, the critic judged <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="87\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>87</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">87\%</annotation></semantics></math> of Python Coding Agent calls incorrect, motivating reusable implementations of these computations. The FREAK tools make visibility, layout, and counting decisions explicit, addressing the evidence-interpretation needs of channel A. The visibility verifier recovered the most gate examples among the three FREAK tools; the table reports generation-stage recovery, not a per-tool benchmark ablation.</p>
</div>
