<span id="A6.p65.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p65.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Task.<span id="A6.p65.pic1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Detect every object of the twenty PascalVOC categories in a photograph of fourteen men posing around a dinner table, and return labelled boxes.</span></span></span>
<span id="A6.p65.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p65.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Why it is hard.<span id="A6.p65.pic1.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> The people overlap heavily, some are visible only as a face between two others, and the table is covered with bottles and plates.</span></span></span>
<span id="A6.p65.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p65.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">How the agent solves it.<span id="A6.p65.pic1.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> After a first pass over the four categories present, it zooms on the crowded table and issues narrower queries, ending with a referring expression for one partly hidden man. The final answer matches 22 of the 23 ground-truth objects.</span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
