<span id="A6.p188.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p188.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Task.<span id="A6.p188.pic1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Box every “package of fresh cut fruit” on a supermarket shelf that holds 53 plastic fruit cups in rows.</span></span></span>
<span id="A6.p188.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p188.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Why it is hard.<span id="A6.p188.pic1.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> The category name as given is unusual; a detector queried with it finds only part of the shelf.</span></span></span>
<span id="A6.p188.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p188.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">How the agent solves it.<span id="A6.p188.pic1.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> It rephrases the category as “fruit cup”, which finds every cup, checks two regions with zooms, and returns 53 boxes that all match. Note that the no-tool answer scores zero only because it used pixel coordinates instead of the requested 0–1000 scale (see the note under the results).</span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
