<span id="A6.p254.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p254.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Task.<span id="A6.p254.pic1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> A street photograph from Paris Fashion Week shows a woman in a beige jacket and an orange scarf (faces are blurred in the benchmark image). Which brand’s show was she attending, and which event and year was it?</span></span></span>
<span id="A6.p254.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p254.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Why it is hard.<span id="A6.p254.pic1.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Nothing in the image names the show; without tools the model guesses a Miu Miu show in 2024.</span></span></span>
<span id="A6.p254.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p254.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">How the agent solves it.<span id="A6.p254.pic1.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> A reverse image search finds no match, so the agent turns the photo into a text description and runs an image search with it. The top result is a street-style gallery titled “What they wore to Hermès” at Paris Fashion Week Fall/Winter 2025, and a page visit confirms the event and season.</span></span></span>
<span id="A6.p254.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p254.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Caveat.<span id="A6.p254.pic1.2.4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> The perception step contributes nothing: the agent zooms on what it takes for a shopping bag, but the OCR reads a Paris litter-bag slogan (“Ensemble rendons Paris propre”). The answer comes from search alone.</span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
