<span id="A6.p318.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p318.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Task.<span id="A6.p318.pic1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> The question, in Chinese, asks: how many years apart are the famous Great-Depression-era event commemorated in the first image and the event shown in the second? The first image is a rusted steel monument in a park; the second is a black-and-white photograph of a fight.</span></span></span>
<span id="A6.p318.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p318.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">How the agent solves it.<span id="A6.p318.pic1.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> It identifies each image with reverse image search and dates each event from the web: the Ford Hunger March of 7 March 1932, and the Ford Strikers Riot of 3 April 1941. One page visit fails with a server error, and the agent recovers with a text search. It answers 9 years. The model reasons in Chinese throughout.</span></span></span>
