<span id="A6.p756.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p756.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">How the agent approaches it.<span id="A6.p756.pic1.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> A reverse image search fails, so the agent hypothesizes a species, <span id="A6.p756.pic1.2.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Castanopsis argentea</span>, tests it with a text search and a Wikipedia visit, finds that the species is native to Java and Sumatra rather than China, rejects it, and searches again at the level of the genus.</span></span></span>
<span id="A6.p756.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p756.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Caveat.<span id="A6.p756.pic1.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> The species is never identified. The four provinces in the final answer first appear in the model’s own reasoning, before any search supports them, and the searches only confirm that the genus is diverse in Yunnan. The answer matches the ground truth, but it is not fully grounded in the retrieved evidence.</span></span></span>
