<span id="A6.p879.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p879.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">What to notice.<span id="A6.p879.pic1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> The question compares distances of two kinds of object along a street, which is easy to misjudge in a single photograph. The harness turns it into arithmetic: depth estimation gives metric depth, grounding gives the crosswalk and every car, and a few lines of code compare them. The detections and the depth map reach the code as data bindings held in memory, <span id="A6.p879.pic1.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">segment_crosswalk</span>, <span id="A6.p879.pic1.1.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">segment_cars</span> and <span id="A6.p879.pic1.1.1.1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">depth_result</span>.</span></span></span>
