<span id="A6.p883.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p883.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Task.<span id="A6.p883.pic1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Name the church in a photograph of a dark Gothic interior with a large baroque altar.</span></span></span>
<span id="A6.p883.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p883.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Why it is hard.<span id="A6.p883.pic1.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Many Gothic churches look alike; without tools the model guesses Antwerp Cathedral.</span></span></span>
<span id="A6.p883.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p883.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">How the agent solves it.<span id="A6.p883.pic1.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Searching the whole photograph and describing it in text return only look-alike churches for eleven calls. The breakthrough is to crop the altarpiece alone and reverse-search the crop, which finds an archive photo of this exact painting; a final text search confirms the church.</span></span></span>
