<span id="A6.p1052.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p1052.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Task.<span id="A6.p1052.pic1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> In a large landscape photograph of a hilltop town, say whether a woman with a backpack is to the left or right of a person wearing a beanie.</span></span></span>
<span id="A6.p1052.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p1052.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Why it is hard.<span id="A6.p1052.pic1.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> The two people stand near a bus on a road far below the town and are only a few pixels tall; without tools the model answers “right”.</span></span></span>
<span id="A6.p1052.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p1052.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">How the agent solves it.<span id="A6.p1052.pic1.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Grounding on the full image cannot separate the two people, so the agent zooms in three times, each time closer, and grounds both people again inside the final crop, where they are large enough to tell apart.</span></span></span>
