<span id="A6.p1139.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p1139.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">What to notice.<span id="A6.p1139.pic1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> The two people are a few pixels tall in the full image. Grounding them there returns almost the same tiny box for both queries (Steps 1 and 2), so it cannot separate them. The model zooms three times, each time closer, and grounds again on the final crop (Steps 6 and 7). There the woman with a backpack gets her own box, and the beanie query returns a second person to her right, so the model answers that she is on the left. The beanie query also returns the woman’s box, so this last step still needs the model’s judgement.</span></span></span>
