<span id="A6.p1143.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p1143.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Task.<span id="A6.p1143.pic1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Seven photographs show one living room from different positions. Of four statements about the room, choose the correct one; two of them give the number of throw pillows, 16 or 12, counting partly covered ones.</span></span></span>
<span id="A6.p1143.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p1143.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Why it is hard.<span id="A6.p1143.pic1.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> The pillows are spread across several views, some appear in more than one view, and some are partly hidden; without tools the model picks 12.</span></span></span>
<span id="A6.p1143.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p1143.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">How the agent solves it.<span id="A6.p1143.pic1.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> It grounds “throw pillows” in each of the four views that show seating, zooms on both halves of the main sofa, and chooses the statement with 16 pillows.</span></span></span>
