<span id="A6.p1220.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:37.98em;">
<span id="A6.p1220.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p1220.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">What to notice.<span id="A6.p1220.pic1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Of the four options, two are pillow counts, so the question reduces to counting throw pillows across seven views of one room, including partly covered ones. The model grounds “throw pillows” in the four views that show seating (11, 3, 3 and 1 detections, 18 in total), then zooms on the two halves of the sofa in view 5. It answers 16, which requires recognizing that some pillows appear in more than one view. That cross-view deduplication is implicit: the model does not write it out.</span></span></span>
