<span id="A6.p1344.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p1344.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">What to notice.<span id="A6.p1344.pic1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> The two points are never visible in the same image, so the distance cannot be read off any one view. The harness supplies the three pieces a metric answer needs: camera poses relating the views (Step 1), metric depth in each view (Steps 2 and 3), and code that back-projects both points into a shared frame (Step 4). The model’s own contribution is to locate the two markers in pixels and to state the computation. Tool results pass to the coding agent as named variables held in memory, such as <span id="A6.p1344.pic1.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">camera_trajectory_result</span> and <span id="A6.p1344.pic1.1.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">depth_result_2</span>, not as text the model must copy.</span></span></span>
