<span id="A6.p1410.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p1410.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">What to notice.<span id="A6.p1410.pic1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> The question asks for the distance from the observer of the first view, but the cabinet is marked only in the third view, taken about 0.7 m behind and 0.5 m to the left (Step 1). Depth read at the marker in view 3 is 2.16 m (Step 4), which is the distance from the wrong camera. The final code run unprojects the marker into view 3’s camera frame and moves it into the observer’s frame with the camera-trajectory extrinsics, giving 2.40 m (Step 5). A run that failed on a missing import (Step 3) is simply retried with a narrower objective.</span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
