<section id="A7" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix G </span>Baseline Reproduction</h2>

<div id="A7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We re-run every baseline ourselves on our benchmark suite using each method’s official implementation (Table <a href="#A7.T25" title="Table 25 ‣ Appendix G Baseline Reproduction ‣ OpenVLHarness: Real World Visual Agentic Tool-Use with Multimodal Memory" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">25</span></a>). All baselines receive exactly the same question text as OpenVLHarness, including each dataset’s answer-format instruction (e.g., “a single integer”, or a JSON list of boxes on a <math id="A7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="A7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1000</annotation></semantics></math> scale for grounding); the only addition is a short answer-format instruction that Codex appends for Qwen3-VL backbones (Appendix <a href="#A7.SS1" title="G.1 Training-Free Harnesses ‣ Appendix G Baseline Reproduction ‣ OpenVLHarness: Real World Visual Agentic Tool-Use with Multimodal Memory" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G.1</span></a>). Their predictions are scored with the same evaluation pipeline and judges. Boxes that a baseline returns in a different coordinate frame, such as pixel coordinates of the model’s resized input, are converted to our normalized format before scoring. Every baseline is evaluated on the full evaluation split. On Qwen3-VL, OctoTools and Visual Sketchpad follow the same three-run protocol as OpenVLHarness (Appendix <a href="#A8" title="Appendix H Run-to-Run Variability ‣ OpenVLHarness: Real World Visual Agentic Tool-Use with Multimodal Memory" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H</span></a>); runs with proprietary backbones and the training-based baselines are single runs. A request that fails or times out counts as incorrect.</p>
</div>
